claim.claim-text:
(i) the core particles are regular or irregular in shape and have a size in the range of 20 nm to 20 µm in terms of average longest dimension;
(ii) the core particles are graphitic, glassy or structureless carbon;
(iii) the carbon nanostructures consist of one or more from the group consisting of fullerenes, single-walled carbon nanotubes, multi-walled carbon nanotubes, and their chemical derivatives; or
(iv) the shell coating on the core particles cover a surface area in the range of 50-100% of the total surface area of the core particles.

(i) a nanotube network with carbon black particles dispersed therein;
(ii) carbon black particles coated with nanotubes; or
(iii) graphitic carbon particles coated with carbon nanostructures.

dispersing carbon nanostructures in a liquid medium to form a dispersion;
blending the dispersion with a particulate solid to form a blend;
wherein the method further comprises:
